<title>USA: MedImmune says RespiGam safe in study.</title>
<headline>MedImmune says RespiGam safe in study.</headline>
<dateline>GAITHERSBURG, Md. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>MedImmune Inc said on Monday that a study cited in this month's Pediatrics journal showed that prophylactic infusions of RespiGam reduced respiratory syncytial virus hospitalizations in premature infants and infants with a chronic lung condition called bronchopulmonary dysplasia.</p>
<p>The company said the treatment was safe and well tolerated in the study.</p>
<p>RespiGam is being launched jointly by MedImmune and American Home Products Corp. RespiGam is manufactured by Massachusetts Public Health Biologic Laboratories.</p>
</text>
